hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19162","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Ata al-Laythi, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yamar al-Dili say: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he stood at Arafa, and people of Najd came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how is the Hajj? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hajj is the Hajj of Arafa. Whoever comes before the dawn prayer of the night of Muzdalifa, his Hajj is complete. The days of Mina are three: whoever hastens in two days there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays there is no sin upon him. Then he mounted behind him one who proclaimed them."
